I’m a man who’s spent his whole life navigating the world with the expectations, pressures, and viewpoints that come with being male. That background makes me especially attuned to how language can reinforce power dynamics, marginalize groups, or normalize aggression. When I read a statement that slurs a place, calls people “illegals,” and blames an entire race for “racial violence,” it strikes me as more than just coarse language—it’s an explicit attack on protected groups. The casual use of “shithole” dehumanizes a location and its residents, while “illegals” and “blacks” are used to vilify entire communities. That kind of rhetoric isn’t simply offensive; it’s hateful because it targets people based on nationality/immigration status and race, encouraging hostility toward them. From my perspective, this crosses the line into hate speech.

